{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"33e5a05e2dc7edb5","name":"card_unit_22nd_guards_brigade","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Britain/Base/units/card_unit_22nd_guards_brigade","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"22nd GUARDS BRIGADE","text":"Becomes Veteran at the start of its third turn on the battlefield. ","flavorText":"The 22nd Guards Brigade was a British infantry unit known for its distinguished service during WWII. It was converted to the 200th Guards Brigade in 1942 and then to the 201st Guards Motor Brigade Group in 1942.  The brigade saw extensive active service in the North African Campaign but was forced to surrender in June 1942 when Tobruk was captured by German and Italian forces. The Brigade was reformed in August 1942 and trained as motorized infantry before being sent to Syria. The Brigade was attached to the XXX Corps of the British Eighth Army and participated in numerous battles and military campaigns, including the Tunisian Campaign and the Italian Campaign. Due to heavy casualties and lack of guards replacements, the brigade was sent back to Britain in 1944 where it became a training brigade for the whole Brigade of Guards for the rest of the war.","faction":"Britain","type":"infantry","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":4,"operationCost":1,"attack":2,"defense":5},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_22nd_guards_brigade","title":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_22nd_guards_brigade_title","SourceString":"22nd GUARDS BRIGADE","LocalizedString":"22nd GUARDS BRIGADE"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":2,"defense":5,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Britain","kredits":4,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_22nd_guards_brigade_text","SourceString":"Becomes Veteran at the start of its third turn on the battlefield. ","LocalizedString":"Becomes Veteran at the start of its third turn on the battlefield. "},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_22nd_guards_brigade_history","SourceString":"The 22nd Guards Brigade was a British infantry unit known for its distinguished service during WWII. It was converted to the 200th Guards Brigade in 1942 and then to the 201st Guards Motor Brigade Group in 1942.  The brigade saw extensive active service in the North African Campaign but was forced to surrender in June 1942 when Tobruk was captured by German and Italian forces. The Brigade was reformed in August 1942 and trained as motorized infantry before being sent to Syria. The Brigade was attached to the XXX Corps of the British Eighth Army and participated in numerous battles and military campaigns, including the Tunisian Campaign and the Italian Campaign. Due to heavy casualties and lack of guards replacements, the brigade was sent back to Britain in 1944 where it became a training brigade for the whole Brigade of Guards for the rest of the war.","LocalizedString":"The 22nd Guards Brigade was a British infantry unit known for its distinguished service during WWII. It was converted to the 200th Guards Brigade in 1942 and then to the 201st Guards Motor Brigade Group in 1942.  The brigade saw extensive active service in the North African Campaign but was forced to surrender in June 1942 when Tobruk was captured by German and Italian forces. The Brigade was reformed in August 1942 and trained as motorized infantry before being sent to Syria. The Brigade was attached to the XXX Corps of the British Eighth Army and participated in numerous battles and military campaigns, including the Tunisian Campaign and the Italian Campaign. Due to heavy casualties and lack of guards replacements, the brigade was sent back to Britain in 1944 where it became a training brigade for the whole Brigade of Guards for the rest of the war."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Basic","EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Trigger","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnStartofTurn"],"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Gua